1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,139
The match ended at midnight. A teammate laughed through

2
00:00:03,139 --> 00:00:06,278
the headset. The small room felt full. Then somebody

3
00:00:06,278 --> 00:00:09,417
said, one more?

4
00:00:09,837 --> 00:00:12,670
He looked at the time. Tomorrow, he had promised

5
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:15,503
to build a birdhouse with his younger brother. There

6
00:00:15,503 --> 00:00:18,336
was room for one last game.

7
00:00:18,756 --> 00:00:21,197
The next match went badly. He did not want

8
00:00:21,197 --> 00:00:23,638
to finish on that feeling. The one after it

9
00:00:23,638 --> 00:00:26,079
was close. He did not want to leave while

10
00:00:26,079 --> 00:00:28,520
they were finding their rhythm.

11
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:32,283
When he finally stopped, the room was silent again.

12
00:00:32,283 --> 00:00:35,627
He set three alarms and pictured himself waking as

13
00:00:35,627 --> 00:00:38,971
someone who had slept enough.

14
00:00:39,391 --> 00:00:42,946
At nine twenty, the phone vibrated. His brother had

15
00:00:42,946 --> 00:00:46,502
sent a photo of an empty workbench. No accusation.

16
00:00:46,502 --> 00:00:50,057
Just two pieces of wood, a pencil, and a

17
00:00:50,057 --> 00:00:53,613
seat he had not filled.

18
00:00:54,033 --> 00:00:57,663
He arrived after the session ended. The caretaker was

19
00:00:57,663 --> 00:01:01,293
stacking chairs. His brother carried the unfinished pieces carefully

20
00:01:01,293 --> 00:01:04,923
home in a bag.

21
00:01:05,343 --> 00:01:08,462
His explanation sounded thin while he was saying it.

22
00:01:08,462 --> 00:01:11,582
His brother nodded. We can do it another time.

23
00:01:11,582 --> 00:01:14,701
That made excuses harder.

24
00:01:15,121 --> 00:01:18,135
Back home, the bag went beside the desk. The

25
00:01:18,135 --> 00:01:21,150
unfinished birdhouse made no sound. It simply waited while

26
00:01:21,150 --> 00:01:24,165
the game loaded.

27
00:01:24,585 --> 00:01:26,582
He liked the game. He liked his friends there.

28
00:01:26,582 --> 00:01:28,579
A good evening on a screen meant something to

29
00:01:28,579 --> 00:01:30,576
him.

30
00:01:30,996 --> 00:01:34,032
The problem was the distance between the evening he

31
00:01:34,032 --> 00:01:37,068
chose and the morning he had promised somebody else.

32
00:01:37,068 --> 00:01:40,104
He had been letting one decision make the other

33
00:01:40,104 --> 00:01:43,140
without admitting the connection.

34
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:47,022
He drew three boxes: one more match, less sleep,

35
00:01:47,022 --> 00:01:50,485
a broken promise. It was the sequence of that

36
00:01:50,485 --> 00:01:53,948
Saturday, not an argument that every person who played

37
00:01:53,948 --> 00:01:57,410
would live the same story.

38
00:01:57,830 --> 00:02:00,774
He opened his brother's message again. For a minute,

39
00:02:00,774 --> 00:02:03,717
he planned a grand apology, followed by a perfect

40
00:02:03,717 --> 00:02:06,660
new schedule. Then he deleted the speech and asked

41
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:09,603
when they could meet.

42
00:02:10,023 --> 00:02:12,806
Thursday after school, his brother replied. He wrote the

43
00:02:12,806 --> 00:02:15,590
time on paper and placed it under the keyboard.

44
00:02:15,590 --> 00:02:18,373
The promise now had a place his eyes would

45
00:02:18,373 --> 00:02:21,157
meet.

46
00:02:21,577 --> 00:02:24,688
That night, he told his teammates he would leave

47
00:02:24,688 --> 00:02:27,800
at eleven. One joked about it. Another said he

48
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:30,911
had an early shift too. The boundary felt less

49
00:02:30,911 --> 00:02:34,023
dramatic once it was spoken aloud.

50
00:02:34,443 --> 00:02:37,827
At ten forty, a match ended. A new one

51
00:02:37,827 --> 00:02:41,211
would run past eleven. His hand moved toward the

52
00:02:41,211 --> 00:02:44,596
button anyway. Reading the clock was easy. Accepting an

53
00:02:44,596 --> 00:02:47,980
unfinished appetite was harder.

54
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:51,959
He wanted a satisfying ending: a win, a rank,

55
00:02:51,959 --> 00:02:55,517
a reason that would make stopping feel obvious. The

56
00:02:55,517 --> 00:02:59,075
game did not owe him that ending. He would

57
00:02:59,075 --> 00:03:02,634
have to choose one himself.

58
00:03:03,054 --> 00:03:05,724
He took off the headset and said goodnight before

59
00:03:05,724 --> 00:03:08,394
his hand could start another queue. His friends continued

60
00:03:08,394 --> 00:03:11,065
without him. It felt like standing outside a lit

61
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:13,735
room.

62
00:03:14,155 --> 00:03:16,930
He went to the kitchen and made something to

63
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:19,705
eat. The apartment had no scoreboard. Nobody praised him

64
00:03:19,705 --> 00:03:22,479
for washing a plate. He washed it because he

65
00:03:22,479 --> 00:03:25,254
would need it tomorrow.

66
00:03:25,674 --> 00:03:28,922
Then he opened the bag. He spread the wood

67
00:03:28,922 --> 00:03:32,170
on the floor and checked what was missing. Sandpaper,

68
00:03:32,170 --> 00:03:35,418
two small hinges, and someone who would actually arrive

69
00:03:35,418 --> 00:03:38,666
when he said he would.

70
00:03:39,086 --> 00:03:41,832
Thursday arrived with rain. On the way to the

71
00:03:41,832 --> 00:03:44,577
workshop, he wanted to go home. Keeping a promise

72
00:03:44,577 --> 00:03:47,323
did not make the bus faster or the weather

73
00:03:47,323 --> 00:03:50,069
more encouraging.

74
00:03:50,489 --> 00:03:53,528
His brother was already there, turning a piece of

75
00:03:53,528 --> 00:03:56,567
wood over in his hands. This time, the second

76
00:03:56,567 --> 00:03:59,606
chair stayed occupied. They measured the base and discovered

77
00:03:59,606 --> 00:04:02,644
their first mistake together.

78
00:04:03,064 --> 00:04:06,414
One side was too short. He reached for a

79
00:04:06,414 --> 00:04:09,763
new piece. His brother suggested changing the design instead.

80
00:04:09,763 --> 00:04:13,113
They argued, tried it, and ended up with a

81
00:04:13,113 --> 00:04:16,462
roof that leaned slightly to one side.

82
00:04:16,882 --> 00:04:20,403
The second diagram had no scores: choose a stopping

83
00:04:20,403 --> 00:04:23,924
time, protect the next commitment, show up. It was

84
00:04:23,924 --> 00:04:27,445
a plan for his own week, not a demand

85
00:04:27,445 --> 00:04:30,965
that he give up everything he enjoyed.

86
00:04:31,385 --> 00:04:34,561
The real afternoon was slower than a game. Tools

87
00:04:34,561 --> 00:04:37,736
needed putting away. Glue needed time. There was no

88
00:04:37,736 --> 00:04:40,911
button that skipped the awkward part where neither of

89
00:04:40,911 --> 00:04:44,087
them knew what to do next.

90
00:04:44,507 --> 00:04:47,781
While the glue dried, his phone lit up. His

91
00:04:47,781 --> 00:04:51,055
teammates were online early. He read the message, answered

92
00:04:51,055 --> 00:04:54,329
that he would join later, and put the phone

93
00:04:54,329 --> 00:04:57,603
back in his pocket.

94
00:04:58,023 --> 00:05:01,253
His brother noticed. He did not say anything about

95
00:05:01,253 --> 00:05:04,484
discipline. He asked whether the doorway was wide enough

96
00:05:04,484 --> 00:05:07,714
for a bird. They measured it, then made the

97
00:05:07,714 --> 00:05:10,945
opening a little larger.

98
00:05:11,365 --> 00:05:14,702
On Friday, he played again. He enjoyed it. At

99
00:05:14,702 --> 00:05:18,040
the agreed time, stopping still felt disappointing. He left

100
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:21,378
anyway, without pretending disappointment meant the evening had been

101
00:05:21,378 --> 00:05:24,716
a mistake.

102
00:05:25,136 --> 00:05:28,323
Another night, he stayed too late. The next day

103
00:05:28,323 --> 00:05:31,510
felt heavy. He did not turn that into proof

104
00:05:31,510 --> 00:05:34,697
that boundaries were pointless. He looked at the moment

105
00:05:34,697 --> 00:05:37,884
he had stopped checking the time.

106
00:05:38,304 --> 00:05:41,322
He moved the reminder outside the game and asked

107
00:05:41,322 --> 00:05:44,341
a friend to say goodbye with him. It would

108
00:05:44,341 --> 00:05:47,360
not make every choice easy. It made the choice

109
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:50,378
harder to lose inside another match.

110
00:05:50,798 --> 00:05:54,162
By the next weekend, the birdhouse was finished. Crooked

111
00:05:54,162 --> 00:05:57,526
roof, uneven paint, working hinges. His brother opened the

112
00:05:57,526 --> 00:06:00,890
little panel twice, simply because they had made something

113
00:06:00,890 --> 00:06:04,254
that opened.

114
00:06:04,674 --> 00:06:07,640
They hung it outside the window. No bird arrived

115
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:10,607
on cue. They stood there anyway, looking at the

116
00:06:10,607 --> 00:06:13,573
small wooden thing in the rain, with nothing to

117
00:06:13,573 --> 00:06:16,540
unlock and nowhere to rank.

118
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:20,080
He did not need to stop enjoying the world

119
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:23,200
on the screen. He needed to leave enough of

120
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:26,320
himself for the world that kept his promises. The

121
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:29,440
next invitation came. He checked tomorrow first.
